# ============================================================
# What must NEVER be committed
# ============================================================
#
# The virtual environment is 473 MB - roughly 45x the size of
# the actual app. It is also machine-specific: it contains
# Windows binaries that would be useless on the Linux container
# Streamlit Cloud runs. requirements.txt is what rebuilds it,
# and that is 20 lines.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Python bytecode - regenerated on every run, never useful to share.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyc

# Accidental file created by a shell redirect. Safe to delete.
$null

# Local Streamlit secrets. If you ever add API keys or connection
# strings they go here, and this line is what keeps them off GitHub.
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# ============================================================
# What IS committed, deliberately
# ============================================================
#
# sample_data/ stays IN the repo - all 10.2 MB of it. It is not
# a cache, it is the app's data source. Notebook 17 exported it
# so the app can run with no Databricks connection at all.
# Without it the deployed app has nothing to show.
#
#   sample_data/*.parquet          the tables
#   sample_data/model/model.joblib the trained model, 1.3 MB
#   sample_data/model/encoders.json      Persona="Loyal" -> 3
#   sample_data/model/feature_order.json the 61 columns, in order
#   sample_data/MANIFEST.json      what was exported, and when
#
# If you ever re-export from notebook 17, re-commit these files
# or the deployed app keeps serving the old model.
